{
 "doc": "d9 rivet: the owner-judged Rivet sheets (n8 verdict page, 2026-11-07) cut into game strips by rivet_frames.py --manifest. base = five facings + three drawn left facings + walk, sprint, roll, claw strike, hit, death; eq_<weapon> = five facings + fire/swing right, toward camera, at rest. Swap a sheet here and re-run (the plasma sword redraw is one line). rivet_eq_<weapon>_left = three drawn left facings holding a one-handed weapon in his right claw (the asset lane's answer to the d9 REQUEST), its own strip so the equipped cells never move. A _left row cuts by component (cc 0): the three left figures stand close and a gun or a spark of one crossed into its neighbour's column cut (a floating bell or flame beside him); p55 electro_baton_left keeps the column cut (its figures split into several large components). rivet_reload_<weapon>[_left] (n9 it11) = the library's claw reload (it137): five facings in the reload pose + the 3-frame reload at 3/4 toward right; fig_h per row = 110 x sqrt(eq dome / reload dome) where the facing cells' dome width is > 5 % off the equipped strip's (half the dome pop, half the height pop: DECISION rivet/reload-pack); act_k height-matches the 3 frames to cell 1 (the same view). n10: the fire or swing band scales by its helmet match to the facings; where the measured ratio left the action figure >7 % off them (a shot shrank him) the row carries act_k set by eye from the strip (DECISION rivet/fire-cell-scale); p70 electro_baton_left carries feet_up so its feet, not the baton tip, stand on the cell floor (FOOT_PX).",
